"VAN DUYN MA:Van Duyn MA is a researcher involved in studies related to dietary therapies for adrenoleukodystrophy.", "FATTY ACID ABNORMALITY:", "QUILOTÓRAX:QUILOTÓRAX is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of lymphatic fluid, specifically chyle, in the pleural cavity. This condition can manifest as a pleural effusion and may lead to symptoms such as dyspnea (difficulty breathing) and cough. Chylothorax can occur spontaneously or as a result of trauma, often linked to surgical procedures or disorders of the lymphatic system. Treatment for QUILOTÓRAX typically involves dietary modifications, including specific diets aimed at managing fat metabolism, as well as various medical interventions. These interventions may include surgical techniques and interventional radiology, depending on the underlying cause of the condition. Overall, careful management is essential to address the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the pleural cavity and to alleviate associated symptoms.", "ASCITIS QUILOSA:Ascitis quilosa is a medical condition characterized by the accumulation of chyle, a lymphatic fluid, in the abdominal cavity. This condition often arises due to the rupture or obstruction of abdominal lymphatic ducts and is typically observed around the fifth postoperative day when patients have begun an oral diet. Ascitis quilosa can lead to significant nutritional deficiencies and may necessitate dietary modifications or surgical intervention. It is associated with various medical conditions and can cause symptoms such as abdominal distension. Treatment approaches for ascitis quilosa may include conservative management or surgical options, depending on the severity and underlying causes. In summary, ascitis quilosa involves the accumulation of lymphatic fluid in the peritoneal cavity, requiring specific medical and dietary management to address the associated complications.", "M.ª NURIA VIRGILI CASAS:M.ª Nuria Virgili Casas is a medical professional involved in the study and treatment of nutritional and metabolic disorders.", "RAFAEL LÓPEZ URDIALES:Rafael López Urdiales is a medical professional contributing to research in clinical nutrition and metabolism.", "EVA MARÍA GARCÍA RAIMUNDO:Eva María García Raimundo is a medical professional focused on nutrition and dietetics in clinical settings.", "MÓNICA MONTSERRAT GIL DE BERNABÉ:Mónica Montserrat Gil de Bernabé is a medical professional working in the field of nutrition and dietetics.", "HOSPITAL UNIVERSITARI DE BELLVITGE:Hospital Universitari de Bellvitge is a hospital located in Hospitalet de Llobregat, Barcelona, specializing in endocrinology and nutrition.", "GAUCHER DISEASE TYPE III:Gaucher disease type III is a genetic disorder that affects the body's ability to break down certain fats, leading to various health complications.", "HURLER SYNDROME:Hurler syndrome is a genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme needed to break down glycosaminoglycans, leading to various physical and cognitive impairments.", "MAROTEAUX-LAMY SYNDROME:Maroteaux-Lamy syndrome is a genetic disorder that affects connective tissue and is characterized by skeletal abnormalities and other systemic issues.", "SLY SYNDROME:Sly syndrome is a rare genetic disorder caused by the deficiency of an enzyme that leads to the accumulation of certain substances in the body, affecting various organs."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}